REQ-PRODUCTION-003,IMPLEMENTED,581,582,,"Composite completion: merged PR #579 implements Handoff/05 section 13 deterministic Phase-3 region×labor-category allocation over canonical LaborSupplyPlan/LaborDemandPlan evidence; PR #582 closes the remaining Handoff/05 section 14 sticky N+1 wage-offer boundary. ProductionUnitState now owns live wageOffer as canonical persistent state, initialized from the opening seed or canonical LaborConfig startingReferenceWage, validated as finite/non-negative, and read by Phase-2 planning instead of immutable scenario seed data. Phase 15 derives regional tightness from requested versus available labor using NumericConfig.quantityEpsilon, applies configured bounded regional wage growth plus bounded per-unit vacancy pressure to ACTIVE units, floors the exponential next offer at explicit next-tick effective minimum-wage evidence, emits deterministic tick-scoped WageOfferUpdate records, and persists them only through an explicit between-tick WorldState transition. src/simulation/wageOfferUpdate.test.ts proves PCL-T9 tight-market increase/slack-market decrease, max-step and vacancy clamps, minimum-wage flooring, ACTIVE/zero-demand semantics, insertion-order invariance, malformed/duplicate/incomplete evidence fail-fast behavior and N+1 persistence without in-tick mutation; src/simulation/productionPlanning.test.ts proves Phase-2 reads the live wageOffer rather than seed.wageOffer. Phase-5 payroll/wage settlement remains REQ-PRODUCTION-004; no persistent employer stock or M5+ behavior is claimed."
